      "summary": [
        {
          "type": "summary_text",
          "text": "Let me write the FB.\n\nLogic: if Trip or !Request or invalid -> Count=0, Ready=FALSE. Else Count = min(qCount+1, Preset); Ready = (Count >= Preset).\n\nNote P3: Ready <-> (Count >= Preset and valid). In invalid case Count=0 so false anyway.\n\nImplementation straightforward.\n\nDeclaration:\nFUNCTION_BLOCK FB_Task\nVAR_INPUT\n Request : BOOL;\n Trip : BOOL;\n Preset : USINT;\nEND_VAR\nVAR_OUTPUT\n Ready : BOOL;\n Count : USINT;\nEND_VAR\nVAR\nEND_VAR\n\nImplementation:\nIF Trip OR NOT Request OR (Preset < 1) OR (Preset > 5) THEN\n    Count := 0;\n    Ready := FALSE;\nELSE\n    IF Count < Preset THEN\n        Count := Count + 1;\n    END_IF\n    Ready := (Count >= Preset);\nEND_IF\n\nCareful: Count is output, retained. But reading Count at scan start gives pre-state. Fine. Note if Count > Preset (shouldn't happen), no increment, Ready true. Fine.\n\nUSINT comparison with literal 1 fine.\n\nCompile."
        }
      ]
    },
